#### pub const fn [flex](#method.flex)(self, flex: [Flex](enum.Flex.html "enum ratatui::layout::Flex")) -> [Layout](../prelude/struct.Layout.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Layout")

The `flex` method allows you to specify the flex behavior of the layout.

##### [§](#arguments)Arguments

-   `flex`: A [`Flex`](enum.Flex.html "enum ratatui::layout::Flex") enum value that represents the flex behavior of the layout. It can be one of the following:
    -   [`Flex::Legacy`](enum.Flex.html#variant.Legacy "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::Legacy"): The last item is stretched to fill the excess space.
    -   [`Flex::Start`](enum.Flex.html#variant.Start "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::Start"): The items are aligned to the start of the layout.
    -   [`Flex::Center`](enum.Flex.html#variant.Center "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::Center"): The items are aligned to the center of the layout.
    -   [`Flex::End`](enum.Flex.html#variant.End "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::End"): The items are aligned to the end of the layout.
    -   [`Flex::SpaceBetween`](enum.Flex.html#variant.SpaceBetween "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::SpaceBetween"): The items are evenly distributed with equal space between them.
    -   [`Flex::SpaceAround`](enum.Flex.html#variant.SpaceAround "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::SpaceAround"): The items are evenly distributed with equal space around them, except the first and last items, which have half the space on their sides.
    -   [`Flex::SpaceEvenly`](enum.Flex.html#variant.SpaceEvenly "variant ratatui::layout::Flex::SpaceEvenly"): The items are evenly distributed with equal space around them.

##### [§](#examples-8)Examples

In this example, the items in the layout will be aligned to the start.

```
use ratatui_core::layout::Constraint::*;
use ratatui_core::layout::{Flex, Layout};

let layout = Layout::horizontal([Length(20), Length(20), Length(20)]).flex(Flex::Start);
```

In this example, the items in the layout will be stretched equally to fill the available space.

```
use ratatui_core::layout::Constraint::*;
use ratatui_core::layout::{Flex, Layout};

let layout = Layout::horizontal([Length(20), Length(20), Length(20)]).flex(Flex::Legacy);
```

