#### pub fn [split](#method.split)(&self, area: [Rect](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect")) -> [Rc](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/rc/struct.Rc.html "struct alloc::rc::Rc")<\[[Rect](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect")\]>

Wrapper function around the [`kasuari`](https://docs.rs/kasuari/0.4.12/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/kasuari/index.html "mod kasuari") solver to be able to split a given area into smaller ones based on the preferred widths or heights and the direction.

Note that the constraints are applied to the whole area that is to be split, so using percentages and ratios with the other constraints may not have the desired effect of splitting the area up. (e.g. splitting 100 into \[min 20, 50%, 50%\], may not result in \[20, 40, 40\] but rather an indeterminate result between \[20, 50, 30\] and \[20, 30, 50\]).

This method stores the result of the computation in a thread-local cache keyed on the layout and area, so that subsequent calls with the same parameters are faster. The cache is a `LruCache`, and grows until [`Self::DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE`](../prelude/struct.Layout.html#associatedconstant.DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE "associated constant ratatui::prelude::Layout::DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE") is reached by default. If the cache is initialized with [`Layout::init_cache()`](../prelude/struct.Layout.html#method.init_cache "associated function ratatui::prelude::Layout::init_cache"), it grows until the initialized cache size.

There is a helper method that can be used to split the whole area into smaller ones based on the layout: [`Layout::areas()`](../prelude/struct.Layout.html#method.areas "method ratatui::prelude::Layout::areas"). That method is a shortcut for calling this method. It allows you to destructure the result directly into variables, which is useful when you know at compile time the number of areas that will be created.

##### [§](#examples-13)Examples

```
use ratatui_core::layout::{Constraint, Direction, Layout, Rect};
let layout = Layout::default()
    .direction(Direction::Vertical)
    .constraints([Constraint::Length(5), Constraint::Fill(1)])
    .split(Rect::new(2, 2, 10, 10));
assert_eq!(layout[..], [Rect::new(2, 2, 10, 5), Rect::new(2, 7, 10, 5)]);

let layout = Layout::default()
    .direction(Direction::Horizontal)
    .constraints([Constraint::Ratio(1, 3), Constraint::Ratio(2, 3)])
    .split(Rect::new(0, 0, 9, 2));
assert_eq!(layout[..], [Rect::new(0, 0, 3, 2), Rect::new(3, 0, 6, 2)]);
```

[Source](https://docs.rs/ratatui-core/0.1.2/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/src/ratatui_core/layout/layout.rs.html#738)

#### pub fn [split\_with\_spacers](#method.split_with_spacers)(&self, area: [Rect](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect")) -> ([Rc](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/rc/struct.Rc.html "struct alloc::rc::Rc")<\[[Rect](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect")\]>, [Rc](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/rc/struct.Rc.html "struct alloc::rc::Rc")<\[[Rect](../prelude/struct.Rect.html "struct ratatui::prelude::Rect")\]>)

Wrapper function around the [`kasuari`](https://docs.rs/kasuari/0.4.12/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/kasuari/index.html "mod kasuari") solver that splits the given area into smaller ones based on the preferred widths or heights and the direction, with the ability to include spacers between the areas.

This method is similar to `split`, but it returns two sets of rectangles: one for the areas and one for the spacers.

This method stores the result of the computation in a thread-local cache keyed on the layout and area, so that subsequent calls with the same parameters are faster. The cache is a `LruCache`, and grows until [`Self::DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE`](../prelude/struct.Layout.html#associatedconstant.DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE "associated constant ratatui::prelude::Layout::DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE") is reached by default. If the cache is initialized with [`Layout::init_cache()`](../prelude/struct.Layout.html#method.init_cache "associated function ratatui::prelude::Layout::init_cache"), it grows until the initialized cache size.

##### [§](#examples-14)Examples

```
use ratatui_core::layout::{Constraint, Direction, Layout, Rect};

let (areas, spacers) = Layout::default()
    .direction(Direction::Vertical)
    .constraints([Constraint::Length(5), Constraint::Fill(1)])
    .split_with_spacers(Rect::new(2, 2, 10, 10));
assert_eq!(areas[..], [Rect::new(2, 2, 10, 5), Rect::new(2, 7, 10, 5)]);
assert_eq!(
    spacers[..],
    [
        Rect::new(2, 2, 10, 0),
        Rect::new(2, 7, 10, 0),
        Rect::new(2, 12, 10, 0)
    ]
);

let (areas, spacers) = Layout::default()
    .direction(Direction::Horizontal)
    .spacing(1)
    .constraints([Constraint::Ratio(1, 3), Constraint::Ratio(2, 3)])
    .split_with_spacers(Rect::new(0, 0, 10, 2));
assert_eq!(areas[..], [Rect::new(0, 0, 3, 2), Rect::new(4, 0, 6, 2)]);
assert_eq!(
    spacers[..],
    [
        Rect::new(0, 0, 0, 2),
        Rect::new(3, 0, 1, 2),
        Rect::new(10, 0, 0, 2)
    ]
);
```

